# FIRESTORE SCHEMA GUARDIAN: INFINITY PROTOCOL v6.2

> Firestore is the backbone. Schema mistakes are permanent and costly. Model once, correctly.

## 1. DOCUMENT MODELING MANDATES
```typescript
// ✅ Canonical document shape — ALL Firestore docs following this structure
interface FirestoreDoc {
  // Core data fields here...
  metadata: {
    createdAt: Timestamp;    // ALWAYS server timestamp
    updatedAt: Timestamp;    // ALWAYS server timestamp
    createdBy: string;       // uid
    isDeleted: boolean;      // Soft-delete flag (default: false)
    version: number;         // Schema version for migrations
  };
}
```
- No arrays of objects for frequently mutated data → use subcollections.
- Document size limit: **1MB hard cap** — never embed full content bodies inline.
- Timestamps: ALWAYS `FieldValue.serverTimestamp()`. Never `new Date()` or `Date.now()`.

## 2. COLLECTION ARCHITECTURE
| Pattern | Use When | Avoid When |
|---|---|---|
| Root collection | Independent entities (users, orders) | Deeply nested relationships |
| Subcollection | Entity has many owned children (user/orders) | Data needed across parents |
| Denormalization | Read-heavy, write-rare data | High write frequency data |
| `_cache/` doc | Aggregations (counts, totals) | — |

## 3. QUERY & INDEX DISCIPLINE
- Composite indexes go in `firestore.indexes.json` — NEVER created ad-hoc in console.
- Avoid `array-contains-any` + `in` in same query (not supported).
- Pagination: ALWAYS use `startAfter(lastDoc)` cursor — never `offset()`.
- Default query limit: **25 docs**. Max: **500**. Never unbounded `.get()` on large collections.

## 4. COST CONTROL
```typescript
// ✅ Aggregation via cached counter (NOT counting documents on every read)
const cache = await db.doc('_cache/analytics').get();
const totalUsers = cache.data()?.totalUsers ?? 0;

// ❌ EXPENSIVE — reads every document to count
const count = (await db.collection('users').get()).size;
```
- Count operations: use `_cache/` aggregation docs updated by Cloud Function triggers.
- Batch writes: max **500 operations** per `writeBatch()`.
- Firestore read budget alerts: set GCP budget alert at **$5 increments**.

## 5. SECURITY RULES SOVEREIGNTY
```javascript
// ✅ Required pattern — server timestamp validation in rules
allow create: if request.resource.data.metadata.createdAt == request.time
  && request.resource.data.metadata.isDeleted == false
  && request.auth != null;
```
- Rules MUST validate: data types, required fields, value ranges, and `isDeleted == false` on creates.
- Test rules with Firebase Emulator. Never deploy untested rules to production.
